title: Psalms 64–65: Hide Me, and Praise Waiteth for Thee
description: Psalms 64 and 65 in the King James Bible: hide me from the secret counsel of the wicked, who whet their tongue like a sword, David's enemies fallen by their own devices, praise waiteth for thee in Sion, our transgressions purged away, the temple of his body, and the river of God, from the Psalms series studies.
