=== Psalm 64
--- Psalm 64 [title]
overline: The Book of Psalms
heading: Psalm 64
sub: Hide me from the secret counsel of the wicked
refs: Psalm 64:1

--- Prayer in troubling times
kicker: Psalm 64 · Hear my voice
scripture: Psalm 64:1-2 | mark: preserve my life from fear of the enemy; Hide me from the secret counsel of the wicked
p: **Psalm 64**, a Psalm of David, another entry in the songbook of prayer to God in troubling times.
p: When we consider the life of David, we see that these two things are true:

--- All that will live godly
kicker: Cross references • Psalm 64:2
scripture: 2 Timothy 3:12-13 | mark: all that will live godly in Christ Jesus shall suffer persecution; evil men and seducers shall wax worse and worse
p: David, the apple of God's eye, a man after God's own heart, had a life of constant tribulation. He had hosts of enemies, foreign and domestic. He sought the will of God most of his life.

--- Constant trouble
kicker: Psalm 64 · The life of David
p: It wasn't perfect. There are none righteous, no not one. He made mistakes and suffered consequences for them. But largely we find David being sought by the wicked for no reason, under threat, the target of arrows, both literal and the figurative arrows of lies, with and without cause.
p: He gained the Kingdom he was anointed to, only after years of flight and fighting. Once established, he saw war and invasion, palace intrigue, the loss of his first son with Bathsheba, the betrayal by his son Absalom, the contention as he approached death and appointed the younger son Solomon to the crown...David saw constant trouble while remaining faithful to the end.

--- The insurrection of the workers of iniquity
kicker: Psalm 64 · Hide me
p: He trusted the Lord God to preserve him in the face of his enemies. To hide him, protecting him from their schemes.
p: While he maintained his respect for Saul, refusing to lay a hand on God's anointed, leaving judgment in God's hands, he was beset by the insurrection of the workers of iniquity who rose up against him as King.

--- They encourage themselves in an evil matter
kicker: Psalm 64 · Bitter words
scripture: Psalm 64:3-6 | mark: Who whet their tongue like a sword; They encourage themselves in an evil matter; They search out iniquities
p: He was often vexed that the evil men and seducers waxed worse and worse, deceiving, and being deceived, but he was never moved. They would encourage themselves in their evil. They would search out iniquity, diligently. Their hearts deep with the evil they sought for him.
p: But his faith never wavered.

--- Their own tongue to fall upon themselves
kicker: Psalm 64 · But God shall shoot at them
scripture: Psalm 64:7-8 | mark: But God shall shoot at them with an arrow; So they shall make their own tongue to fall upon themselves
p: He trusted God to deliver him. To destroy his enemies as He destroyed Goliath, Saul, the Philistines, Amalekites, Ammonites, Arameans/Syrians and Edom. His son's insurrection, the betrayal of Ahithophel, Sheba, son of Bichri who led a rebellion by the Benjaminites, his trusted general Joab and High Priest Abiathar, who both backed David's eldest son, Adonijah over Solomon, even lowly Shimei, son of Gera who cursed David as he fled the revolution of Absalom.

--- Each fall by their own devices
kicker: Psalm 64 · Their own end
p: These men who whetted their tongues like a sword, sharpening their words like a blade, would fall upon themselves. Their slander and schemes against David would be their own end.
p: David faced endless betrayal and danger, and through it all sought the face of God, and saw each fall by their own devices while David remained protected by the Lord he called upon.

--- Surely as He delivered David
kicker: Psalm 64 · Trust in Him
scripture: Psalm 64:9-10 | mark: The righteous shall be glad in the LORD, and shall trust in him
p: Psalms like this remind us to place our faith in the Lord. That our eternal soul is already given to Him, bought with a price paid for by Jesus, sealed unto redemption by the Spirit, the earnest of our inheritance. Our spirit crying out to the Father, "Abba!"
p: If we have trusted God for eternity, how can we fear the temporal slings and arrows of life's outrageous fortune? The vanity of men who seek our destruction? Surely as He delivered David, He will deliver us. We can place our trust in His strong tower, to be gathered under His wing. To be still and know He has us in His hand.
center: Amen

=== Psalm 65
--- Psalm 65 [title]
overline: The Book of Psalms
heading: Psalm 65
sub: Praise waiteth for thee, O God, in Sion
refs: Psalm 65:1

--- Unto thee shall all flesh come
kicker: Psalm 65 · Praise waiteth for thee
scripture: Psalm 65:1-2 | mark: O thou that hearest prayer, unto thee shall all flesh come
p: David's Psalm of praise and glory to God contains doctrine and prophecy. Acknowledging the power of the Lord, the weakness of man, the need for salvation and the blessings on His people, in this life and in eternity.
p: The praise of Christ, coming into His own in Zion, the promises fulfilled. *O thou that hearest prayer, unto thee shall all flesh come.* Every knee shall bow and tongue confess, that Jesus is Christ.

--- Thou shalt purge them away
kicker: Psalm 65 · Iniquities prevail against me
big: Psalm 65:3 | mark: thou shalt purge them away
p: Iniquities may prevail in our flesh, but our sins will be purged away.

--- Sin that dwelleth in me
kicker: Cross references • Psalm 65:3
scripture: Romans 7:15-20 | mark: it is no more I that do it, but sin that dwelleth in me
p: The flesh at war with the Spirit, gives way to the purging that comes in Christ.

--- O wretched man that I am
kicker: Cross references • Psalm 65:3
scripture: Romans 7:24-25 | mark: I thank God through Jesus Christ our Lord

--- Blessed is the man whom thou choosest
kicker: Psalm 65 · Thy holy temple
big: Psalm 65:4 | mark: Blessed is the man whom thou choosest, and causest to approach unto thee
p: But blessed is the man who through Jesus Christ our Lord is made to come before Him, into His courts to dwell forever in the goodness of His house, even of His holy temple. His body, given for us.

--- The temple of his body
kicker: Cross references • Psalm 65:4
scripture: John 2:19-22 | mark: But he spake of the temple of his body

--- The tabernacle of God is with men
kicker: Cross references • Psalm 65:4
p: And in the eternal forever of the new Heaven and the New earth, when the sons of God present themselves before God, we shall rejoice at the vow being kept.
scripture: Revelation 21:3-4 | mark: Behold, the tabernacle of God is with men

--- The Lamb is the temple of it
kicker: Cross references • Psalm 65:4
scripture: Revelation 21:22-23 | mark: the Lord God Almighty and the Lamb are the temple of it
center: [[Revelation 21:3-5|Read Revelation 21:3–5]]

--- Terrible things in righteousness
kicker: Psalm 65 · O God of our salvation
big: Psalm 65:5 | mark: By terrible things in righteousness wilt thou answer us
p: Terrible things in righteousness, spoken of The Lord;

--- It is done
kicker: Cross references • Psalm 65:5
scripture: Revelation 21:5-8 | mark: I will give unto him that is athirst of the fountain of the water of life freely; the second death
p: The God of our salvation, in Whom all our confidence is, from the four corners of the earth shall we come, believers, to be taught of God.

--- Which stilleth the noise of the seas
kicker: Psalm 65 · The power of Creation
scripture: Psalm 65:6-8 | mark: Which stilleth the noise of the seas, the noise of their waves, and the tumult of the people
p: The power of Creation, the Lord of the raging seas. Who calms our hearts as He does the tumult of the storm.

--- A great calm
kicker: Cross references • Psalm 65:7
scripture: Matthew 8:26-27 | mark: rebuked the winds and the sea; and there was a great calm
p: How much more the storm of our heart?
big: Revelation 21:4

--- The river of God
kicker: Psalm 65 · Thou visitest the earth
scripture: Psalm 65:9-10 | mark: the river of God, which is full of water; thou makest it soft with showers
p: The Lord and Savior visited the earth, and streams of living water pour out from Him, the Spirit inside us, ever flowing, the harvest ready.

--- Rivers of living water
kicker: Cross references • Psalm 65:9
scripture: John 7:38-39 | mark: out of his belly shall flow rivers of living water
p: He is glorified in the resurrection, and made to sit in heavenly places, making the ground fertile and the furrows of man's heart, soft, able to receive the seed of the word, and be made to spring forth from the ground as the fruit of corn.

--- They shout for joy, they also sing
kicker: Psalm 65 · Thou crownest the year
scripture: Psalm 65:11-13 | mark: Thou crownest the year with thy goodness; they shout for joy, they also sing
p: He makes the flocks lay down in green pastures, the hills themselves rejoice, the corn is abundant, white for the harvest. That we may glorify God, shouting for joy and singing of the mercies of the Lord forever. Amen

